---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { page } from "../lib/asset";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — codescribe"
  description="How codescribe handles audio, transcripts, AI requests, and system permissions. Local by default; cloud only when you opt in."
  path="privacy"
>
  <LegalPage title="Privacy Policy" eyebrow="Trust · Privacy" updated="2026-10-06">
    <p>
      Codescribe supports local speech recognition. Optional cloud transcription,
      AI formatting, agent tools, and spoken replies use the services you configure.
      This page describes which data those paths can send and what stays on your Mac.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy summary</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Data</th>
          <th>Where it goes</th>
          <th>Your control</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Audio</strong></td>
          <td>Your Mac only</td>
          <td>Sent to a transcription provider when cloud STT is enabled</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Transcripts</strong></td>
          <td>Local history; configured AI services when used</td>
          <td>Stored under <code>~/.codescribe/transcriptions/</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>AI requests</strong></td>
          <td>Your chosen provider</td>
          <td>Only if AI formatting / agent features are enabled</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Telemetry</strong></td>
          <td>Nowhere</td>
          <td>No transcript analytics SDK; update and service requests are separate</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>What stays local</h2>
    <p>
      The app keeps these local files and credentials. Requests to configured
      services are described below:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Whisper model</strong> — runtime-resolved local path/cache; local
        STT runs on-device.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Audio recording</strong> — complete local captures, preserved even
        when transcription or delivery fails. Settings › Audio › Audio retention
        defaults to Forever; choices are Forever / 30 days / 7 days / 24h / Off.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Transcripts</strong> — <code>~/.codescribe/transcriptions/</code
        >; you control retention.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Configuration</strong> — settings plus optional <code
          >~/.codescribe/.env</code
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>API keys</strong> — macOS Keychain (and/or restricted local config).
      </li>
      <li><strong>Prompts</strong> — <code>~/.codescribe/prompts/</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Once the local speech models and permissions are ready, recording, local
      transcription, hotkeys, and text delivery can run without a cloud AI service.
      Model downloads, updates, and licence issuance need a network connection.
    </p>

    <h2>What can leave your Mac (opt-in only)</h2>
    <h3>Optional AI formatting / agent calls</h3>
    <p>
      When you enable AI formatting or agent features, transcribed text (not
      audio) is sent to the provider you configure. Built-in remote providers use HTTPS;
      custom endpoints use the configured transport. That may be
      OpenAI-compatible Responses/chat endpoints, Anthropic, a self-hosted stack
      such as LibraxisAI, or local Ollama. Formatting sends transcript text and
      instructions. Agent requests may also include the conversation history,
      selected text, files, screenshots, and tool results used for your task.
    </p>
    <h3>Optional spoken replies</h3>
    <p>When a remote speech provider is selected, reply text is sent to that
      provider to produce audio. Its privacy policy and usage charges apply.</p>
    <h3>Optional cloud STT</h3>
    <p>
      If you turn off local STT and configure a cloud STT endpoint, audio may be
      sent after capture for a final transcript. Live preview still stays local
      in the current product shape.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Cloud is never required for core dictation. Maximum-privacy setups disable
      AI formatting, force local STT, and leave LLM endpoints unset.
    </p>

    <h2>System permissions (TCC)</h2>
    <p>macOS may ask for:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Microphone</strong> — record speech while you hold a hotkey or start
        a session.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Accessibility</strong> — paste text and interact with the focused
        app when you ask it to.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Input Monitoring</strong> — detect modifier/hotkey state (not a keylogger
        of content).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Speech Recognition</strong> — when using Apple’s speech path for a live
        transcript.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Screen Recording permission enables screenshots when used as context.
      Agent tools can read files within their configured workspace and permissions.
      Review the selected agent and provider before attaching sensitive material.</p>

    <h2>Tracking and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The desktop app does not ship a third-party transcript analytics SDK.
      Update checks contact the configured Sparkle feed, model downloads contact
      their download hosts, and optional AI services contact their providers.
      Website analytics are disabled in the default site build; a deployment can
      enable them explicitly.
    </p>

    <h2>Website licence issuance</h2>
    <p>The licence form sends your email over HTTPS to the Codescribe licence
      service. The service signs a code containing a SHA-256 hash of the normalized
      address. Its issuance log records that hash, the client IP address, and a
      timestamp. A hash is a pseudonymous identifier, not anonymous data. The app
      verifies the signed licence locally.</p>
    <h2>Data retention and rights</h2>
    <p>
      Audio lives locally under <code>~/.codescribe/takes/</code>,
      <code>~/.codescribe/sessions/</code>, and the daily
      <code>~/.codescribe/transcriptions/</code> archive. Finite retention expires
      completed owned audio after processing and read leases settle. Off applies
      to future takes and does not erase old recordings. Active takes keep their
      starting choice; uncertain completion or failed deletion preserves audio
      and records an error. Audio retention does not delete transcript text.
      Transcript history lives under <code>~/.codescribe/</code>. You can
      disable history, delete files, or remove the whole directory. For EU users
      under GDPR-style access/erasure/portability requests: your data is already
      on your Mac as plain files you control. We do not operate a cloud account
      that holds your dictation history by default.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Codescribe is built by Vetcoders / LibraxisAI. Questions: <a
        href="mailto:hello@vetcoders.io">hello@vetcoders.io</a
      >
      · <a href={page("support")}>Support</a>
      · source at
      <a
        href="https://github.com/vetcoders/codescribe"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/vetcoders/codescribe</a
      >.
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
